  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's start by understanding Sophia's request. She wants to book a one-way flight from ORD to PHL on May 26, same as her previous flight on May 10. She's adding an extra passenger, Kevin Smith, and doesn't want any bags. She's okay with economy class but wants aisle and middle seats together. She's willing to pay up to $500; if it's over, she'll drop the second passenger. No insurance, and she wants to pay with a certificate only.\n\nFirst, I need to get the details of her previous reservation from May 10 to replicate the flight. So, I should call get_user_details with her user ID to find that reservation. Once I have the reservation ID, I can get the flight details. Then, check the availability for May 26. If the same flight is available, proceed. Next, calculate the cost for two passengers in economy, including any extra fees. If the total exceeds $500, adjust to one passenger. Then, book using her certificate. Also, ensure the seats are adjacent (aisle and middle). Need to confirm all steps with her before proceeding.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_user_details\", \"arguments\": {\"user_id\": \"sophia_silva_7557\"}}\n",
